# JWT Reference — VTC Apps

Bootstrap flow: `auth-bootstrap.mdc`. Lib exports: `lib-canonical.mdc`.

## Standard claims

| Claim | Example | Notes |
|-------|---------|--------|
| `iss` | `tag_api_v1` | Issuer |
| `aud` | `zapi_server` | Audience |
| `iat` / `exp` | unix seconds | Validate `exp` on server |
| `user_id` | `"1"` | Matches URL `user` |
| `user_type` | `"1"` | Platform user type |
| `initial_login_user_id` | `"1"` | Original login user |
| `user_name` | `"mark"` | Username slug |
| `group_id` | `"2"` or `"0"` | Matches URL `group`; `"0"` = personal context — `personal-storage.mdc` |
| `group_user_name` | `"vtc"` | Space slug in space context |
| `role` | object | Space context; see below |
| `client_id` | string | Client/session id |
| `network_id` | string | Network context |
| `token_id` | string | Token instance id |

Never trust URL `user`/`group` without verifying against decoded JWT.

## Server verification (required)

Decoding the payload (base64, `jwt.decode`, `decodeJwt`, jose `decodeJwt`) does **not** check the
signature. Anyone can build a token with any `user_id`, `group_id` or `role`. On the server:

- Get the user with `const user = await getAuthenticatedUser(request)` from `@/lib/auth`.
- `getAuthenticatedUser` confirms the token with the VTC API: `GET {VTC_API_URL}/api/v1/auth/verify`
  with `Authorization: Bearer <token>` → 200 `{ data: { claims } }` for a genuine token, 401 for a
  forged, tampered or expired one. Use `@vtc/auth` with `{ requireVerified: true }` (fail closed:
  if the API cannot be reached, refuse the request). Cache results briefly (valid ≤ 5 min, invalid
  30 s); never past `exp`.
- No `JWT_SECRET`, no module credential in the app. `/api/v1/users/me` does not exist — do not use it.
- Only then compare URL `user`/`group` with the claims and check `role` for admin actions.
- Client-side decode stays for display only.

## Space context — role object

```json
{
  "user_id": "1",
  "group_id": "2",
  "group_user_name": "vtc",
  "role": {
    "role_id": "5464",
    "role_name": "Member",
    "role_type": "3"
  }
}
```

Owner example: `"role_type": "1"`, `"role_name": "Owner"`.

## AuthenticatedUser type

```typescript
export type AuthenticatedUser = {
  user_id: string
  user_type: string
  initial_login_user_id: string
  user_name: string
  group_id: string
  group_user_name?: string
  role?: { role_id: string; role_name: string; role_type: string }
  client_id?: string
  network_id?: string
  token_id?: string
}
```

## Parent app localStorage (reference — do not read from child apps)

`app.vtc.com` shell localStorage keys (legacy names): `posif_auth_state`, `posif_groups_state`, `posif_client_unique_id`, `posif_settings`.
